From: DKR-R Windows 95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Pause the game by holding back its retraces

The Windows 95 port pauses the game while its window has lost the
foreground (E06-S01). The VI thread asks the port before each retrace,
through a weak dkr_game_paused(): while it answers non-zero, no retrace
is sent. DKR advances on retraces, so its logic, race clock and audio
stop where they are; the retrace count follows the clock, so nothing is
owed when the pause ends. A screen update is queued at each change of
state, which wakes the graphics thread so that the port's renderer can
hand the screen to the desktop and take it back. A build without the
symbol never pauses.
---
--- a/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
@@ -498,6 +498,9 @@
 extern std::atomic_bool exited;
 // The steps of the shutdown, marked without I/O (librecomp/src/recomp.cpp).
 extern "C" void dkr_stop_mark(unsigned bit);
+// Non-zero while the port wants the game paused (patch 0065); weak, so a build
+// without it never pauses.
+extern "C" int dkr_game_paused(void) __attribute__((weak));
 extern moodycamel::LightweightSemaphore graphics_shutdown_ready;
 
 void set_dummy_vi(bool odd);
@@ -568,6 +571,24 @@
         }
         total_vis = new_total_vis;
 
+        /* Patch 0065: the port pauses the game by holding back its retraces.
+           DKR advances on them, so its logic, race clock and audio stop where
+           they are, and since the count above follows the clock, nothing is
+           owed when the pause ends: one retrace, as after any late wake. The
+           screen update sent at each change of state wakes the graphics
+           thread, which hands the screen to the desktop and takes it back. */
+        {
+            static bool was_paused = false;
+            const bool paused = dkr_game_paused != nullptr && dkr_game_paused() != 0;
+            if (paused != was_paused) {
+                was_paused = paused;
+                events_context.action_queue.enqueue(ScreenUpdateAction{ events_context.vi.regs });
+            }
+            if (paused) {
+                continue;
+            }
+        }
+
         // If the game hasn't started yet, set a dummy VI mode and origin.
         if (!ultramodern::is_game_started()) {
             static bool odd = false;
